-- (6, 2, 5): all 377 primitive solutions of a^6 + b^6 = c^6 + d^6 + e^6 + f^6 + g^6
-- with every term below 250000, from R. Gerbicz, J.-C. Meyrignac and U. Beckert,
-- arXiv:1108.0462 (submitted 2011-08-02). Reported by Anders, who sent the list.
--
-- Additive: 352 new rows, new contributors and resources, one search claim, and
-- guarded updates of the 25 rows already on the site. Every identity was
-- recomputed with exact integers, is primitive, and matches the paper's appendix
-- row for row; ids use the appendix number (boinc-625-NNN).
--
-- Credit: the appendix's "discoverer's name" for each solution, verbatim (two
-- names where the BOINC workunit was computed twice). The one exception is the
-- name the paper prints as '????' (rows 244, 263, 275, 307, 369): yoyo@home's
-- list of found solutions (https://www.rechenkraft.net/yoyo/y_euler_solutions.php) shows the same
-- partner and timestamp with the volunteer 前朝遗少 (user 26222) in all five.
--
-- Dates, the earliest each solution is documented:
--   * 1117^6 + 770^6 = ...: 1999 (found by Brisse and Resta in 1999, per the
--     paper's introduction; year only, so 1 January).
--   * the other 24 with a1, a2 < 20000: 2002-06-06, the electronic publication of
--     Resta and Meyrignac, Math. Comp. 72 (2003) 1051-1054, whose Table 1 lists
--     exactly these 25. (2003 is the print volume year.)
--   * the remaining 352: the date of the earliest record of the solution on
--     yoyo@home's list of found solutions, which logs every BOINC find with its
--     time (April 2010 - July 2011). For the 228 solutions new to the BOINC
--     runs (largest term above 88000, two names in the paper) this is their
--     discovery. The other 124 were found earlier by Meyrignac's distributed
--     project (1999-2010) on dates no surviving source gives, so their first
--     BOINC record is the earliest documented date. The paper itself gives no
--     dates per solution. yoyo@home is attached to these rows as a source.
--
-- Rows rewritten: the 25 existing (6, 2, 5) rows credited 'Resta and Meyrignac 2003'
-- get the appendix credit and the date above, and their tool link moves from
-- the GitHub copy of the Resta-Meyrignac paper to the arXiv paper (the DOI of
-- Resta-Meyrignac is kept on them as a source). Nothing is deleted.

